// trap: a goal holds on the base values of a deleted row.
// Flag sets `held`, and only Drop ends a held order, by deleting it. The deleted row's
// `held` is its base value, false, so the goal holds after the delete, and Drop is fair:
// the property holds. A checker that read the goal as "present and not held" would see the
// goal never hold and report a counterexample.
// expect HeldReleased: native=ok tlc=ok
entity Order "注文" { id: Int @pk  held: Bool @default(false) }
usecase Place "注文"
usecase Flag "保留"
usecase Drop "削除"
creates(Place, Order)
sets(Flag, Order.held == true)
deletes(Drop, Order)
condition Held "保留中"
holds(Held, Order.held == true)
applies_to(Held, Drop)
property HeldReleased leads_to(Order.held == true, Order.held == false).fair(Drop)
